---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Cookies"
  description="Dustbound cookie policy — dustbound.app sets no first-party cookies and uses no analytics."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6" data-testid="cookies-page">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-black text-ink">Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 21 August 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-muted" data-testid="cookies-body">
      <p data-testid="no-first-party-cookies">
        The Dustbound website at <a href="https://dustbound.app/">dustbound.app</a> <strong class="text-ink">does not set first-party cookies</strong> and <strong class="text-ink">does not use analytics</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because we do not use non-essential cookies or tracking scripts, we do not show a cookie consent banner.
      </p>
      <p>
        Store buttons on this site are ordinary links to Google Play and the App Store. They do not set Dustbound cookies.
        The Support form posts to Formspree so we can reply; that is a submission, not a Dustbound cookie.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages (and any CDN such as Cloudflare in front of the site) may process standard technical connection data
        (for example IP address and User-Agent) when serving pages. That is hosting infrastructure, not Dustbound first-party cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we later add analytics or third-party challenge scripts, we will update this policy and add consent where required.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
